WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Most people who want to quit their job

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.560
think that they need investors and a

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.000
business plan or some kind of special

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.640
skill to make it happen. But today I'm

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.360
going to show you these six businesses

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.840
that you can start for under a thousand

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.680
dollars that have a real path to

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.760
replacing your income. Not as a side

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.320
hustle, but as an actual career. My name

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.200
is Austin Zeeback and I've been building

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.760
businesses for over a decade in real

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.840
estate, pest control, and a handful of

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.880
other industries. And every business on

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.880
this list is something that I've seen

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.480
firsthand actually work. And if you get

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.160
any value out of today's video, do me a

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.560
huge favor and just smash that like

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.840
button. It'll really help us out a ton

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.040
and get this video in front of more

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.480
people who need to see it. Let's start

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.360
with one that's going to surprise you.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.160
And most people have no idea that this

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.360
is even a business, let alone one that

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.960
generates recurring subscription revenue

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.440
every single month. And that is

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.240
can-to-curb services. You take people's

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:48.560
trash cans from their garage or their

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.840
backyard to the curb on collection day

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.680
and then you bring it back. That's

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.400
literally the entire business. And I

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.080
actually did a full business tour with

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.640
the founder of a company called Can

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.280
Monkey, which is an Arizona-based

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.360
company built around this exact idea.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.080
And he told me the entire origin story.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.640
He was walking his dog one night when he

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.120
watched his neighbor pull up in his

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.960
Mercedes, drive straight into the

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:09.200
garage, and leave the trash cans sitting

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.160
at the end of the driveway. And he

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.120
realized that nobody wants to deal with

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.520
this annoying task. Maybe there's an

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.640
opportunity here. And that one

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.600
observation became a real business. And

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.400
Can Monkey is not a small company. They

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.640
actually rank number two in consumer

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.480
services of Inc. 5000's list of

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.360
America's fastest growing companies.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.840
They've been featured on ABC News and

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:31.280
they now service over 6000 properties.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:33.000
They handle more than 30,000 individual

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.200
bin movements every single month and

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.840
they operate across 25 states and

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.600
hundreds of cities. And they charge

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.400
between 45 and 65 dollars a month per

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.360
property depending on the plan. And the

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.200
model works because it solves a problem

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.080
that sounds small until you actually

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.480
have it solved for you and then you can

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.560
never go back. And that is the

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.760
psychology that makes this business so

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.680
powerful. The churn rate on subscribers

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.280
is almost nothing. Once somebody has

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.200
this handled for them, the monthly

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.800
charge kind of becomes invisible. And

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.640
it's the same reason that people never

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.000
cancel their housekeeper or their pool

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:05.400
cleaner. Convenience is addictive. Now,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.240
think about the customer base for a

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.560
minute. Elderly homeowners who can't

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.280
drag heavy cans down a long driveway in

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:13.120
the heat or in the cold. Busy dual

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.240
income families who forget until they

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.640
hear the truck at 6:00 in the morning,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.880
and then they scramble out there in

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.160
their pajamas. And corporate

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.400
professionals who value their time more

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.040
than the cost of the service itself. And

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.240
then there's this one. The United States

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.840
has around 2.25 million active Airbnb

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.240
properties. And every single one of

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.000
